.TH LLM-MANAGER-RESTORE-REVIEW 8 "2026-09-06" "LLM-Manager" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
llm-manager-restore-review \- inspect and save a system restore review
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec /usr/bin/llm-manager-restore-review list
.PP
.B pkexec /usr/bin/llm-manager-restore-review preview
.I backup-id
.PP
.B pkexec /usr/bin/llm-manager-restore-review approve
.I request-sha256 canonical-request-hex
.PP
.B pkexec /usr/bin/llm-manager-restore-review status
.I request-id request-sha256
.SH DESCRIPTION
This dedicated privileged entry inspects an existing root-owned Ollama backup
and current fixed drop-in, or saves a matching immutable review.
It does not restore settings or restart services.
The request is the dedicated manual-restore protocol, encoded as lowercase hex,
limited to 16 KiB before encoding. Arguments contain metadata, never settings.
The helper independently validates caller identity, host, origin, encrypted
backup, target state, hashes and expiry. Hashes alone do not authorize execution.
.PP
List returns at most 32 canonical root-owned backup summaries for the independently
resolved local host, sorted by backup ID. It reads no key or current target and
returns no ciphertext hash, key ID or payload. Orphan, partial, unknown, changing
or excessive store entries reject the entire inventory; results are never silently
truncated. Selecting a summary is not review or execution authority.
.PP
Status reads immutable execution history after checking the independently
resolved caller UID, host and exact request hash under one shared store lock.
Expired reviews remain readable. Status needs only the execution store, not
keys, backup payloads or the current target. It never reserves or retries work.
Review-only means no attempt record was observed; it is not execution authority.
An attempt without a result is unknown and requires attention. Missing, unsafe
or incomplete evidence is an error, never proof that no mutation occurred.
Committed describes the recorded outcome, not current service health.
.SH SECURITY
The review-system-restore PolicyKit action requires fresh administrator
authentication for an active session. The Apply action is not used.
Only the package-installed isolated Python launcher should be used.
Root-owned stores and keys must already exist; no directories or keys are
created by this command. Missing or unsafe stores fail closed.
The explicit GUI workflow keeps inventory selection, review consent and final
execution consent as separate steps. The normal production route remains gated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/llm-manager/local-root-restore
Fixed root-owned backup, key and execution stores.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates a preview, saved review or successful history read. Inspect the
returned state; a successful status command does not imply a committed restore.
1 indicates a rejected or unavailable review; 2 indicates invalid CLI syntax.
